            <ArticleTitle>Basic Methods for Isolating and Culturing Microalgae.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/7651_2017_99</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this chapter, I go through the very basic methods for isolating and setting up a microalgae culture. Isolation can be done from local algal strains with a micropipette and microscope. Determining algal growth is important and can be done by counting cells under a microscope or by determining the change in dry weight (DW).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
